       "PRINCIPLE_MULTIPLE_REPRESENTATIONS"
      ],
      "rationale": "Number names include ones with a zero place, such as five hundred one, where the spoken name gives no word for the missing tens.",
      "misconceptions": [
       "Writes five hundred one as 51 or 5001.",
       "Writes the teen part in spoken order, such as 571 for five hundred seventeen."
      ],
      "references": [
       "Common Core Standards Writing Team (2015), Progressions for the Common Core State Standards in Mathematics, K–5, Number and Operations in Base Ten"
      ]
     },
